  "_doc": "[wild] Ambient animals (fauna/fauna.gd, rules in fauna/fauna_rules.gd, meshes in fauna/fauna_models.gd). regions: city (ordinary city districts), wild (ordinary wilderness districts), or a frontier biome id (dust_flats, frozen_port, sunken_city, cradle_landing). where: land, water (a lake/flood hex), shore (a land hex next to water), district (anywhere; count is per district). levels [min, max]: hex level (0 Junk, 1 Clean, 2 Planted, 3 Growing, 4 Sustained, 5 Thriving); hub ground counts as level 1. junk: true = only on hexes that still have junk (rats; fewer as the hex is cleaned), false = clean ground only. edge: only Sustained+ hexes at the edge of the restored area (deer). time: any, day or night. per_hex [min, max] animals on a qualifying hex (flock size for birds, school size for fish); chance: share of qualifying hexes that get them. cap: most of this species in a district. coats: tints for the coat mask (variety). kind picks the behaviour. Water species also need the lake hex cleaned; fish numbers grow with lake clarity (research).",
